// Native K: letting p index the token within a page and i index into
// head_size, k is indexed as [p * head_size + i], one row of head_size bf16
// values per token. Packed K: see Note [K VNNI storage].

body:
**[comments] Rule 2, restates identifiers: shorten**

'k is the typed owner k_vnni_tensor' and '(TRON_K_VNNI, 128-dimension heads)' restate the std::conditional_t on k_vnni::layout_on, and 'Both hold page_size * head_size bf16 values' restates the static_assert two lines below ('packed K holds the same bytes as native K'). The last sentence explains what std::conditional_t does with the unselected type, a language fact (Rule 6); if a reviewer asks why k_vnni_tensor's static_assert does not fire for other head sizes, answer in the review.

Proposed:
```cpp
  // Native K: letting p index the token within a page and i index into
  // head_size, k is indexed as [p * head_size + i], one row of head_size bf16
  // values per token. Packed K: see Note [K VNNI storage].
```

Line-to-code mapping (Rule 4):
lines 1-2 and 'values per token.' -> `using native_k_storage = bf16[page_size * head_size];`; 'Packed K: see Note [K VNNI storage].' -> `using k_storage = std::conditional_t<k_vnni::layout_on<head_size>, k_vnni_tensor<...>, native_k_storage>;`; the two static_asserts carry their own messages
